{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"tool_name\":\"final\",\"arguments_json\":\"{\\\"response\\\":\\\"contract_version: 0.1.0\\\\nartifact_version: 1\\\\nwork_item: \\\\\\\"20260908T113118\\\\\\\"\\\\nobservable_behaviour:\\\\n  - id: planner-derived-inputs\\\\n    behaviour: \\\\\\\"The deterministic planner derives absent required, material, and applicable conditional-material inputs from the pinned question policy and assembled request, independently of StructuredIntent.missing_material_inputs.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - id: conditional-distance\\\\n    behaviour: \\\\\\\"For VC-POC-05, VC-POC-06, and VC-POC-07, distance_km is required only when market_definition is distance.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - id: safe-transactional-school-resolution\\\\n    behaviour: \\\\\\\"Each named school must resolve to exactly one directory record; IDs are staged in mention order, deduplicated without reordering, and committed to Deps only after all mentions resolve.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - id: exact-selector-shapes\\\\n    behaviour: \\\\\\\"Single-school questions submit one acara_sml_id; multi-school questions submit ordered unique acara_sml_ids; VC-POC-04 requires at least two distinct IDs.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - id: metric-normalization-routing\\\\n    behaviour: \\\\\\\"Requested selectors are Unicode-safe case-folded and separator-normalized, canonical values and pinned aliases are accepted, order-preserving deduplication is applied, and selectors are routed to the question-specific field and static vocabulary.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - id: smallest-schema-valid-request\\\\n    behaviour: \\\\\\\"The planner constructs a fresh request from explicit intent values and the applicable planner-owned selectors, omits unsupplied defaults, and validates it against the registered pinned request schema before evidence dispatch.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - id: explicit-filter-constraints\\\\n    behaviour: \\\\\\\"VC-POC-09 and VC-POC-10 require an explicit cohort-defining filter: absent, empty, or sector-default-only definitions clarify, while unknown nested keys fail before dispatch.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - id: bad-request-origin-separation\\\\n    behaviour: \\\\\\\"Unnormalizable user selectors and invalid caller-supplied numeric identities clarify; planner/schema defects and unexpected bad_request responses after deterministic validation raise TerminalError; none becomes Unsupported.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - id: default-cli-pipeline\\\\n    behaviour: \\\\\\\"The default CLI invokes converse with no legacy agent so that ask(deps, question) executes the four-stage deterministic pipeline, while explicit legacy-agent callers remain supported.\\\\\\\"\\\\nrequired_outputs:\\\\n  - path: \\\\\\\"harness/planner.py\\\\\\\"\\\\n    result: \\\\\\\"Deterministic policy derivation, transactional identity resolution, static selector normalization and routing, pinned-schema validation, exact request construction, explicit-filter enforcement, and origin-aware error handling.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - path: \\\\\\\"run.py\\\\\\\"\\\\n    result: \\\\\\\"Default CLI wiring selects the deterministic pipeline without constructing or passing a legacy agent.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - path: \\\\\\\"tests/unit/test_planner.py\\\\\\\"\\\\n    result: \\\\\\\"Focused coverage of input derivation, school resolution, selector normalization, all-question schema validation, explicit-filter constraints, exact requests, and error-origin semantics.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - path: \\\\\\\"tests/unit/test_intent_boundary.py\\\\\\\"\\\\n    result: \\\\\\\"Pipeline coverage proving clarification bypasses narration, validated requests reach evidence, and planner failures propagate without becoming Unsupported.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - path: \\\\\\\"tests/unit/test_run_cli.py\\\\\\\"\\\\n    result: \\\\\\\"CLI coverage proving the default path does not build or pass a legacy agent and selects the deterministic pipeline signature.\\\\\\\"\\\\ndeterministic:\\\\n  - id: full-test-suite\\\\n    repo: k-12Harness\\\\n    command: \\\\\\\".venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -q\\\\\\\"\\\\n    expected: \\\\\\\"The complete deterministic suite exits zero with no failures and no unexpected passes.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    expect:\\\\n      exit_code: 0\\\\n      stdout_excludes: \\\\\\\"xpassed\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - id: affected-modules\\\\n    repo: k-12Harness\\\\n    command: \\\\\\\".venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/unit/test_planner.py tests/unit/test_intent_boundary.py tests/unit/test_run_cli.py -q\\\\\\\"\\\\n    expected: \\\\\\\"All affected test modules collect and pass.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    expect:\\\\n      exit_code: 0\\\\n      stdout_excludes: \\\\\\\"failed\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - id: focused-nonvacuous-acceptance\\\\n    repo: k-12Harness\\\\n    command: \\\\\\\".venv/bin/python -m pytest -q tests/unit/test_planner.py::test_missing_market_definition_is_derived_without_model_hint tests/unit/test_planner.py::test_distance_is_conditional_on_distance_market tests/unit/test_planner.py::test_ambiguous_school_clarifies_without_fetch tests/unit/test_planner.py::test_metric_normalization_and_exact_profile_request tests/unit/test_planner.py::test_vc_poc_03_routes_selector_to_ratios tests/unit/test_planner.py::test_unknown_request_property_fails_before_fetch tests/unit/test_planner.py::test_peer_filters_require_explicit_nondefault_filter tests/unit/test_planner.py::test_segment_filters_reject_unknown_nested_key tests/unit/test_planner.py::test_schema_valid_emitter_bad_request_is_terminal tests/unit/test_planner.py::test_invalid_explicit_identity_bad_request_clarifies tests/unit/test_intent_boundary.py::test_planner_failure_is_not_unsupported tests/unit/test_run_cli.py::test_main_uses_pipeline_path_by_default\\\\\\\"\\\\n    expected: \\\\\\\"Every named acceptance test exists, collects, and passes; a missing or renamed test makes the command fail.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    expect:\\\\n      exit_code: 0\\\\n      stdout_excludes: \\\\\\\"failed\\\\\\\"\\\\nmust_not_change:\\\\n  - \\\\\\\"The legacy PydanticAI agent-tool repair loop, its repair ceiling, and its replay compatibility behaviour.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - \\\\\\\"Evidence-contract files, PINNED.json, registry contents, request or response schemas, and the captured input-catalog snapshot.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - \\\\\\\"The evidence client protocol, runtime emitter, database access, or evidence calculations.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - \\\\\\\"Answer-view, narration, rendering, grounding, confidence, limitations, claim eligibility, or contract-owned refusal wording.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - \\\\\\\"The prohibition on School_No to ACARA_SML_ID crosswalks.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - \\\\\\\"contract.material_inputs_for() and the unchanged legacy O-8 strict xfail.\\\\\\\"\\\\nfailure_behaviour:\\\\n  - condition: \\\\\\\"A named school has zero or multiple directory matches.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    expected: \\\\\\\"Return ClarificationNeeded for that school, record the preflight, make no evidence call, and retain no partial resolved-ID mutation.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - condition: \\\\\\\"Explicit school IDs conflict with name-resolved identities.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    expected: \\\\\\\"Raise TerminalError before evidence dispatch and retain no partial identity update.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - condition: \\\\\\\"Deduplication leaves fewer than two identities for VC-POC-04.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    expected: \\\\\\\"Return ClarificationNeeded without evidence dispatch.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - condition: \\\\\\\"A required or applicable material user-selectable field is absent.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    expected: \\\\\\\"Return ClarificationNeeded in stable pinned-policy order, with contract field names and static allowed values where available, without evidence dispatch.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - condition: \\\\\\\"A requested static selector cannot be normalized to the applicable pinned vocabulary.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    expected: \\\\\\\"Return ClarificationNeeded with the applicable static vocabulary and make no evidence call.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - condition: \\\\\\\"A planner-built request violates its registered schema, contains an unknown top-level or nested field, or cannot load or resolve its pinned schema safely.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    expected: \\\\\\\"Raise TerminalError before evidence dispatch; do not return Unsupported.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - condition: \\\\\\\"VC-POC-09 or VC-POC-10 lacks an explicit nondefault cohort-defining filter.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    expected: \\\\\\\"Return ClarificationNeeded without evidence dispatch.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - condition: \\\\\\\"A locally validated request containing only a caller-supplied numeric ACARA identity receives bad_request.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    expected: \\\\\\\"Record the failed fetch invocation and return identity clarification.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - condition: \\\\\\\"Any other locally validated deterministic request receives bad_request.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    expected: \\\\\\\"Record the failed fetch invocation and raise TerminalError containing the question ID and emitter context.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - condition: \\\\\\\"The emitter returns unknown_question, excluded_question, or unanswerable.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    expected: \\\\\\\"Preserve the established typed abstention and contract-owned reason semantics without retry.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - condition: \\\\\\\"The emitter returns data_unavailable or internal.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    expected: \\\\\\\"Raise TerminalError as an operational failure.\\\\\\\"\\\\ncompatibility:\\\\n  - \\\\\\\"Excluded-topic, registry-owned exclusion, gated-question, unknown-question, and unanswerable outcomes retain their established typed outcomes and contract-owned text.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - \\\\\\\"Successful complete, partial, and empty envelopes remain successful and are stored unchanged in deps.last_envelope.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - \\\\\\\"Well-typed release-derived and open values that match no facts remain successful empty or partial results, not schema failures.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - \\\\\\\"Every directory preflight and evidence invocation, including failed invocations, remains observable in deps.tool_calls.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - \\\\\\\"The deterministic planner's TerminalError handling remains distinct from the legacy model-driven repair-once loop.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - \\\\\\\"converse() continues to accept an explicit legacy agent for replay and compatibility tests.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - \\\\\\\"CLI credential selection, emitter selection, rendering, clarification limit, and exit-code behaviour remain unchanged.\\\\\\\"\\\\ncompatibility_baselines:\\\\n  - source: \\\\\\\"contract/POC_CONTRACT_V0.3_SPEC.md\\\\\\\"\\\\n    revision: \\\\\\\"sha256:065f2a38b4befc09363b300cf7d601e4e782175ae6ef1ebca24d4eb173dfbe57\\\\\\\"\\\\n    obligation: \\\\\\\"Preserve v0.3 request validation, default ownership, error taxonomy, and static-versus-release-derived semantics.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - source: \\\\\\\"contract/poc_question_registry.v0.3.0.json\\\\\\\"\\\\n    revision: \\\\\\\"sha256:3bea2093b2e900ecf7b27528aaad1dcec93f11791dd87ccf85c67f73f588b7cb\\\\\\\"\\\\n    obligation: \\\\\\\"Use registered input policies, request-schema references, availability rules, metric lists, and VC-POC-09/10 constraints.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - source: \\\\\\\"contract/question_schemas/v0.3.0/_index.json\\\\\\\"\\\\n    revision: \\\\\\\"sha256:e5b9877ffeb14e436433ebbc894de62a4bf8022324b9a33cfc80f4538d09bb1d\\\\\\\"\\\\n    obligation: \\\\\\\"Preserve required, material, conditional-material, defaultable, optional, support, and gating classifications.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - source: \\\\\\\"contract/poc_input_catalog.v0.3.0.schema.json\\\\\\\"\\\\n    revision: \\\\\\\"sha256:41bad353798aa0c2dbbd2fcc33db806430a12c371db8c20ef35d822aac207dc2\\\\\\\"\\\\n    obligation: \\\\\\\"Use its question-field mapping and embedded static enums without enum-enforcing release-derived or open values.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - source: \\\\\\\"prompts/input_catalog.snapshot.json\\\\\\\"\\\\n    revision: \\\\\\\"sha256:a53480e98cca27a64518dbb940c6e83a69270132aa20b491874bb2b68f10fe10\\\\\\\"\\\\n    obligation: \\\\\\\"Retain consistency with captured canonical vocabularies without adding a runtime catalog dependency.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - source: \\\\\\\"prompts/rules.md\\\\\\\"\\\\n    revision: \\\\\\\"sha256:6a2a92d5ddba792b56c450ded4a2a982d04530b557967ab129c50fa37fb06d28\\\\\\\"\\\\n    obligation: \\\\\\\"Preserve smallest-request behaviour and the pinned teaching staff to teaching_fte alias.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - source: \\\\\\\"evals/cases/golden_cases.json\\\\\\\"\\\\n    revision: \\\\\\\"sha256:10587743a8041e1d0520951e5b308a4776a2f462d0dae6f84a74cd9ce9632d92\\\\\\\"\\\\n    obligation: \\\\\\\"Preserve existing answer, clarification, refusal, gated, empty-success, and injection-resistance expectations.\\\\\\\"\\\\ncontract_requirements:\\\\n  - id: manifest-allowlist-conflict\\\\n    requirement: \\\\\\\"The amended plan requires run.py and tests/unit/test_run_cli.py, but manifest scope.declared_files lists only harness/planner.py, tests/unit/test_intent_boundary.py, and tests/unit/test_planner.py. Execution must not begin until the human reviewer expands the manifest diff allowlist to include the two additional required outputs.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - id: pinned-policy-authority\\\\n    requirement: \\\\\\\"Planner policy and schema routing must come from hash-pinned v0.3 artefacts, not a new hand-maintained per-question policy.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - id: complete-schema-validation\\\\n    requirement: \\\\\\\"Every constructed request for every registered question must validate against its registered pinned Draft 2020-12 request schema before dispatch, including additionalProperties, nested keys, types, bounds, uniqueness, cardinality, conditionals, and formats.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - id: safe-schema-resolution\\\\n    requirement: \\\\\\\"Only registered request-schema paths beneath the pinned contract directory may be loaded; load or reference-resolution failures are TerminalError.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - id: policy-order\\\\n    requirement: \\\\\\\"Clarification fields are stable across runs and follow pinned required, material, then applicable conditional-material order.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - id: known-condition-only\\\\n    requirement: \\\\\\\"Only the exact pinned distance_km condition for VC-POC-05/06/07 is interpreted; an unknown conditional expression is contract drift and raises TerminalError.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - id: no-invented-defaults\\\\n    requirement: \\\\\\\"Unsupplied defaultable values are omitted so the emitter remains owner of defaults and resolved_request.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - id: preflight-boundary\\\\n    requirement: \\\\\\\"A school-directory record establishes identity only and supplies no campus, catchment, geography-crosswalk, or School_No evidence.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - id: static-vocabulary-source\\\\n    requirement: \\\\\\\"Static selector routing uses registry metric_list and the input-catalog schema's question-field mapping and embedded enums; it does not call the runtime emitter for contract-static lists.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - id: direct-id-authority-conflict\\\\n    requirement: \\\\\\\"golden_cases.json permits explicit ACARA ID 99999 to bypass directory lookup and yield empty success, while the v0.3 specification says an ID absent from the pinned directory is bad_request. Preserve the plan's bounded resolution: do not add directory preflight for caller-supplied numeric IDs, and treat a resulting bad_request as identity clarification until the Definition Pack owner resolves the conflict.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - id: od07-explicit-filter-rule\\\\n    requirement: \\\\\\\"Enforce the registry-owned VC-POC-09/10 explicit-filter constraint in addition to JSON Schema without creating a general condition language.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - id: invocation-recording\\\\n    requirement: \\\\\\\"Record every completed directory preflight and every evidence attempt, including failed attempts, before returning or raising.\\\\\\\"\\\\nsemantic:\\\\n  - id: no-model-missing-input-trust\\\\n    criterion: \\\\\\\"VC-POC-05 without market_definition clarifies even when the model reports no missing input, and irrelevant model-reported missing fields are ignored.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - id: conditional-materiality\\\\n    criterion: \\\\\\\"An SA2 market request does not ask for distance_km, while a distance market without distance_km does.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - id: transactional-identity\\\\n    criterion: \\\\\\\"Each school contributes an ID only after exactly one match; mention order is preserved, duplicates are removed, and a later failed match leaks no partial state or request.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - id: exact-profile-normalization\\\\n    criterion: \\\\\\\"For VC-POC-01, Total Enrolments and teaching staff become total_enrolments and teaching_fte without adding headcount or non-teaching metrics.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - id: exact-ratio-routing\\\\n    criterion: \\\\\\\"VC-POC-03 staffing-intensity selectors use the ratios vocabulary and ratios request field, with no metrics property.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - id: exact-comparison-request\\\\n    criterion: \\\\\\\"VC-POC-04 dispatch contains ordered unique IDs, explicitly requested canonical metrics, and only other explicitly supplied schema fields; emitter-owned year defaults remain omitted.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - id: schema-and-filter-fail-closed\\\\n    criterion: \\\\\\\"Unknown top-level or nested properties, invalid shapes, and impossible planner-produced requests fail before dispatch; VC-POC-09/10 missing or default-only cohort definitions clarify.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - id: bad-request-origin\\\\n    criterion: \\\\\\\"Caller-correctable identity problems clarify, while planner defects and unexpected post-validation bad_request responses fail operationally; neither is rendered as an unsupported question.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - id: production-routing\\\\n    criterion: \\\\\\\"run.py main does not call build_agent for its default execution and passes None to converse, while tests that pass an explicit agent continue to use the legacy path.\\\\\\\"\\\\nout_of_scope:\\\\n  - \\\\\\\"Re-parsing raw natural language in Stage 2; determinism is defined for identical StructuredIntent values.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - \\\\\\\"Conditional-material expressions beyond the exact pinned distance_km condition.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - \\\\\\\"General synonym inference beyond mechanical normalization and explicitly pinned aliases.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - \\\\\\\"Directory-membership preflight for caller-supplied numeric ACARA IDs while the Definition Pack conflict remains unresolved.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - \\\\\\\"Fuzzy school matching, ranking, match confidence, or selecting among ambiguous records.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - \\\\\\\"A new batch directory protocol.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - \\\\\\\"Changes to the legacy agent-tool repair loop or its output semantics.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - \\\\\\\"Changes to contract artefacts, the emitter, database, answer view, narration, rendering, graders, or presentation semantics.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - \\\\\\\"New evidence capabilities, sources, crosswalks, catchments, campus locations, transport, finance, capacity, outcomes, or forecast execution.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\"}\"}"}}
